  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 707.03 Operation Requirements",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 707.03 Operation Requirements.\n\n(a) Operators of existing facilities shall comply with the following operation requirements:\n\n(1) 40 CFR 265.12, required notices;\n\n(2) 40 CFR 265.13, general waste analysis;\n\n(3) 40 CFR 265.14, security;\n\n(4) 40 CFR 265.15, general inspection requirements;\n\n(5) 40 CFR 265.16, personnel training;\n\n(6) 40 CFR 265.17, general requirements for ignitable, reactive, or incompatible wastes, including those wastes or materials listed in 40 CFR 265 Appendix V;\n\n(7) 40 CFR 265.19, construction quality assurance program;\n\n(8) 40 CFR 265, Subpart C, preparedness and prevention;\n\n(9) 40 CFR 265, Subpart D, contingency plan and emergency procedures;\n\n(10) 40 CFR 265, Subpart F, groundwater monitoring;\n\n(11) 40 CFR 265, Subpart G, closure and post-closure; and\n\n(12) Subject to (b), below, 40 CFR 265, Subpart H, financial requirements.\n\n(b) The liability insurance required pursuant to 40 CFR 265.147(b)(1), identified in (a)(12), above, shall be as specified in 40 CFR 264.147(b)(1)(i) and (ii).\n\nSource. #5053, eff 1-24-91; ss by #5886, eff 8-26-94; ss by #7207-B, eff 2-26-00; ss by #7333, eff 8-1-00; ss by #7578, eff 10-13-01; (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Hw 700) ss by #9367, eff 1-28-09; amd by #10205, eff 10-19-12; ss by #12349, eff 8-14-17 (formerly Env-Hw 707.02)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw700.html"
